<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Mesh Description</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="101.026%" size="4" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Meshes are 3D structures generated from raw scan data. Each mesh entity consists of <b>vertices</b> that are connected in <b>triangles</b>. Some of the meshes may contain isolated groups of triangles.</span></p>
<p class="Example"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for mesh surface</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP291349008" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs4">
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">Triangles and vertices forming the surface of meshes</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../../User_Interface/Menus/Visualisation_menu_files/image002.jpg" width="683px" height="473px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Every vertex is connected with at least one triangle, which means that a mesh cannot contain isolated vertices. There is no limit for the triangles sharing one vertex. An indication for regular mesh is when most of the vertices connect six triangles.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for regular mesh</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP1796637928" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../../User_Interface/Menus/Visualisation_menu_files/image003.gif" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Every triangle defines a normal that is used for the rendering. The normal is a vector, which is orthogonal to the plane where the triangle lays. When you are in</span> <span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Flat Shaded</u></span> <span lang="EN-GB">or</span> <span class="Mode" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Smooth Shaded</u></span> <span lang="EN-GB">rendering mode, triangles, which normals face towards the viewport, are shaded. Triangles, which normals face backwards the viewport, are in different colour. Some of the processing functions deal with point normals. The point normal is an average of the normals of the surrounding triangles.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a3" style="text-decoration:underline;">Examples for meshes in different rendering modes</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP300024265" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs4">
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-decoration:none;"><span><span style="text-decoration:none;"><span lang="EN-GB">Mesh in</span> <u><span lang="EN-GB" style="text-decoration:none;">Points</span> r</u><span lang="EN-GB">endering mode</span></span></span></p>
<p class="whs9"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../../User_Interface/Menus/Visualisation_menu_files/image005.jpg" width="397px" height="293px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt=""></span></p>
<p class="whs9">&#160;</p>
<p class="whs9"><span lang="EN-GB">Mesh in Wireframe rendering mode.</span></p>
<p class="whs9"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../../User_Interface/Menus/Visualisation_menu_files/image007.jpg" width="396px" height="292px" border="0" class="img_whs11" alt=""></span></p>
<p class="whs9">&#160;</p>
<p class="whs9"><span lang="EN-GB">Mesh in Flat Shaded rendering mode.</span></p>
<p class="whs9"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../../User_Interface/Menus/Visualisation_menu_files/image029.jpg" width="396px" height="292px" border="0" class="img_whs11" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">All rendering modes are available for displaying meshes – see</span> <u><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="visualisation.htm">Visualisation</a></span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">for details. Different triangles can be distinguished</span> <span class="Mode">Wireframe</span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span class="Mode">Flat</span><span lang="EN-GB">, and</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Flat + Wireframe</u></span> <span lang="EN-GB">render modes.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><a href="javascript:void(0);" onclick="var e; if (parseInt(navigator.appVersion)&gt;=4){e=event;} if (parseInt(navigator.appVersion) &gt;=2 &amp;&amp; typeof(PopupMenu_Invoke) == 'function') PopupMenu_Invoke(e,'','Mesh Menu','../../User_Interface/mesh_menu.htm','Rendering Flat and Flat Mode','../../References/Rendering_Flat_and_Flat_Shaded_Mode.htm','Rendering Smooth and Smooth Mode','../../References/Rendering_Smooth_and_Smooth_Shaded_Mode.htm');return false;" title=""><img src="../../add_on/ss_btn_see_also.gif" border="0" height="17" width="60" alt=""></a></b></span></p>
